---
import Document from '../../layouts/Document.astro';
import { localeParams } from '../../lib/i18n';
import { VERSION } from '../../lib/levels';
export const getStaticPaths = localeParams;
const { lang } = Astro.props;
---

<Document lang={lang} path="/project" translated={false}
  title="Project status — AI Usage Scale"
  description="Definitions, governance, implementation evidence and the current review status of the AI Usage Scale."
  breadcrumb={[["Project status", "/project"]]}
  navLabel="Project status" sections={[
    { href: '#overview', label: 'Scope and stewardship' },
    { href: '#references', label: 'Public references' },
    { href: '#standards', label: 'Standards discussion' },
    { href: '#review', label: 'Review and next steps' }
  ]}>
  <header slot="header">
    <p class="label">Independent proposal · v{VERSION}</p>
    <h1>Project status</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">A shared vocabulary for describing how generative AI contributed to a work.
      Definitions, tools and the evidence behind the project.</p>
  </header>

  <section id="overview">
    <h2>Scope and stewardship</h2>
    <dl class="project-facts">
      <div><dt>Vocabulary</dt><dd>6 levels</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Core languages</dt><dd>22</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Definitions &amp; marks</dt><dd>CC0</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>The scale provides six definitions, a decision procedure, downloadable marks and
      machine-readable data. English is the normative source. A declaration records a
      publisher's account of the process; it does not certify quality, rights or legal compliance.</p>
    <p>Konrad Karauda maintains the project in
      <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale">the public repository</a>.
      Decisions and contribution routes are documented in the
      <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md">governance</a>
      and <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">contribution guide</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="references">
    <h2>Public references</h2>
    <p>Evidence checked on 10 October 2026. These records show references and integration interest;
      an independent production declaration has not yet been verified.</p>
    <ul class="reference-list">
      <li>
        <div><a href="https://github.com/chaoss/disclosure#other-ai-disclosureattribution-tools">CHAOSS disclosure</a><span class="label">Related tool</span></div>
        <p>The scale is listed among other AI disclosure and attribution tools.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div><a href="https://github.com/chaoss/wg-ai-alignment/blob/main/moderation/README.md#tools">CHAOSS AI Alignment</a><span class="label">Resource list</span></div>
        <p>A second reference from the same community, in its moderation resources.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div><a href="https://github.com/voxpelli/diarie/blob/main/.diarie/tasks/tasks-backlog.yml">diarie</a><span class="label">Deferred integration</span></div>
        <p>The public backlog records adoption interest and a question about the Level 3 / Level 4 boundary.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>To record a use, provide a public declaration in
      <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale/blob/main/docs/ADOPTERS.md">the adoption evidence file</a>.
      Using the scale requires no signature, registration or account.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="standards">
    <h2>Standards discussion</h2>
    <p>Schema.org's <a href="https://schema.org/DefinedTermSet">DefinedTermSet</a> and
      <a href="https://schema.org/DefinedTerm">DefinedTerm</a> describe the vocabulary.
      Work declarations use an explicit project extension for <code>aiUsageLevel</code>.</p>
    <p>The relevant public venues are
      <a href="https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg/issues/3391">Schema.org's AI disclosure discussion</a>
      and the <a href="https://www.w3.org/groups/cg/ai-content-disclosure/">W3C AI Content Disclosure Community Group</a>.
      Follow the <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale/issues/11">submission and pilot record</a>
      for requests, responses and implementation evidence.</p>
    <p>The scale remains an independent proposal. Suggested mappings do not imply institutional
      acceptance. Google lists its supported features in the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/search-gallery">Search gallery</a>;
      a dedicated feature for these levels is not documented there.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="review">
    <h2>Review and next steps</h2>
    <dl class="review-list">
      <div><dt>Editorial review</dt><dd>The October revision was developed with AI. Human editorial review is pending.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Translation review</dt><dd>The 21 translations are labelled as machine translations awaiting fluent human review.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Classification boundary</dt><dd>The Level 3 definition requires meaningful review, but its current decision path stops before asking about it. An automated Level 3 result is provisional.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>The next priorities are independent pilots, fluent language reviewers and a documented
      decision on the review boundary. See the
      <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md">roadmap</a>.
      The <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale/blob/main/docs/history/manifesto-2026-07.md">original July rationale</a>
      is retained in the historical archive.</p>
  </section>
</Document>
